      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The first image shows a fallback from a shader that doesn’t have a _Ramp property. The result appears flat.\n\nThe second image shows a fallback from a shader with _Ramp explicitly set to ShadowRampRealisticSoft.png, resulting in nice shading.\n\nI would like to achieve the nice shading like the latter, even when falling back from a shader that does not have a _Ramp property.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-23T13:38:12.317Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, when using VRCFallback with toonstandard, the fallback shader may appear flat if the original shader doesn't define a _Ramp property, as no ramp texture is assigned by default.\n\nIt would be helpful to support specifying the shading mode directly in the fallback tag, such as toonstandard_realistic or toonstandard_realisticsoft. This would allow the appropriate built-in ramp to be applied automatically, improving visual consistency in fallback scenarios.",
